course: dictionary
lesson: 11367
title: Shortened words
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: When a word is abbreviated, it has been made shorter. A long word or phrase is written in a short form, so it takes less space and less time to write. «Mr» is the abbreviated form of «Mister».
explain: Abbreviated is also a form of the verb abbreviate, which means to make something shorter. The verb has many forms: abbreviate, abbreviates, abbreviated, abbreviating. «Please abbreviate the title on your poster.»
explain: Abbreviated can also mean shortened in time or length. «The teacher gave us an abbreviated version of the story, with only the main events.» The story is shorter, but the main events are still there. Read the words around the word to decide which meaning fits.
fact: Abbreviated means made shorter.
fact: «Mr» is an abbreviated form of «Mister».
fact: In maths and science, «cm» is an abbreviation of centimetre, and «kg» is an abbreviation of kilogram.
fact: «e.g.» is an abbreviation of «for example».
fact: An abbreviated version of a story keeps the main events but leaves out the extra details.
exercise: «Mr» is the abbreviated form of which word? | Mirror | *Mister | Mountain | Mrs
exercise: «The teacher gave us an abbreviated version of the long book.» What does abbreviated mean here? | Longer and more detailed | Coloured in red | *Shorter, with the main parts kept | Written in a foreign language
exercise: Find and copy the abbreviated word in this sentence: «Please write the length in cm on your worksheet.» | *cm | write | worksheet | length
test: «We wrote e.g. instead of for example in our notes.» What does e.g. show? | *An abbreviation of for example | A question mark | A full sentence | A type of maths unit
test: Ben's text says, «See u at 4, pls be on time.» Why are the words abbreviated? | *Text messages often use short forms to save time | Because he cannot spell at all | To make a poem | Because the phone is broken
exam: What does abbreviated mean? | Made longer and more detailed | *Made shorter, especially in a short written form | Hidden from view | Made bright and shiny
